    <textTemplates>
        <description>when defines the condition that triggers the rule:

- field — the API name of the field to check
- operator — either HAS_VALUE (field is not blank) or EQUALS (field matches a specific value)
- value — only needed when operator is EQUALS

require is a list of field API names that become required when the condition is met.

You can have as many rules in the array as you need. If you only want always-required fields with no conditions, use the Always-Required Fields input instead and just pass a comma-separated string like Cost__c, Notes__c.</description>
        <name>ConditionalRequiredRulesJsonExample</name>
        <isViewedAsPlainText>true</isViewedAsPlainText>
        <text>[
  {
    &quot;when&quot;: {
      &quot;field&quot;: &quot;Status__c&quot;,
      &quot;operator&quot;: &quot;EQUALS&quot;,
      &quot;value&quot;: &quot;Active&quot;
    },
    &quot;require&quot;: [&quot;Cost__c&quot;, &quot;Notes__c&quot;]
  },
  {
    &quot;when&quot;: {
      &quot;field&quot;: &quot;Cost__c&quot;,
      &quot;operator&quot;: &quot;HAS_VALUE&quot;
    },
    &quot;require&quot;: [&quot;Approved_By__c&quot;]
  }
]</text>
